  "text": "Thank you all for your reports. Let me synthesize what I'm hearing and outline the path forward. We have a hard deadline of 5:00 p.m. on October 9, 2026, per Thomas's confirmation with the judge's clerk. Nadia has identified 23 copied files in the Alpha repository and build scripts, which gives us our forensic foundation. Marcus, the client's position is clear — no bar on the engineer working for the competitor, but we must seek return and deletion of the 23 files and a prohibition on their use. Sofia, the insurance coverage requirements are critical and need immediate attention. Before I can approve this application, I need two things resolved: first, Sofia, we need to ensure the insurer receives notice before any court filing — that's non-negotiable for preserving coverage. Second, the question of written insurer consent for outside forensic expert fees needs to be addressed. Nadia, was your forensic work done in-house or through an outside expert? That will determine whether the consent requirement has already been triggered. I want to move quickly, but we cannot sacrifice coverage compliance in the process. Can we get insurer notice out today?"
}
